research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/adhm-gaga-analytic-scaffold.md-69-Statement: Assume AC. For 0≤r≤3 and any coherent analytic O_{P^r(C)}-module F, every H^q(P^r(C),F), q≥0, is finite-dimensional. With the locally defined coherent-section Fréchet topology and the induced Čech quotient topology these cohomology groups are Hausdorff. The proof includes the required Fréchet open-mapping and Schwartz compact-complex finiteness results, local coherent-section topology, and compactness of restriction; none is presumed to follow from a Banach-only or one-variable theorem.
