# GAGA A1: analytic prerequisites and exact proof obligations

Investigation date: 2026-10-23. Assigned scope: read-only examination of the current batch-59 GAGA analytic package. This dossier is the only authored file. It does not certify a proof, approve a new pair, alter imported suppliers, or discharge GAGA A2. Root owns any canonical repair. Repository instructions read: root CLAUDE.md/README.md and physics CLAUDE.md/README.md/SCHEMA.md. The inspected checkout's recent log included 62e7fe36a8, 0a7d267e16, 81e817e2e8; no historical resume document was used as evidence of active completion.

## Disposition

The complete inspected `items/thm-qftx-projective-gaga-for-monad-data.md` has an unconditional public statement but explicitly conditional proof. Its A1 includes a false phrase, “coherent analytic sheaves on projective space and its hyperplanes satisfy Cartan Theorems A and B.” Untwisted Cartan A/B belong on Stein spaces; projective generation and vanishing require sufficiently positive twists. Even after this wording repair, A1 remains a substantial authoring obligation. Existing scalar Dolbeault solvability and Noetherian germ rings do not supply Oka coherence, coherent Cartan A/B, compact coherent cohomology finiteness, or projective uniform generation.

For projective dimension r≥1, O(-1) has no nonzero holomorphic global sections, while its stalks are rank-one nonzero modules, disproving untwisted A. Also H^r(P^r,O(-r-1))≅C, disproving untwisted B. These are independent analytic facts: Demailly VII §10, Theorems 10.6–10.7, printed/PDF pp.348–349, actually read below. The latter also follows from analytic Serre duality and K=P^r's O(-r-1). On a zero-dimensional hyperplane the obstruction disappears; it remains for P²/P³ themselves and their positive-dimensional hyperplanes. Do not invoke GAGA to prove this counterexample while auditing GAGA.

A sound unresolved boundary separates: (i) local faithful flatness and coherence; (ii) scalar analytic projective O-cohomology plus sheaf/Dolbeault comparison; (iii) coherent acyclicity on Stein coordinate domains where actually used; (iv) compact coherent finiteness; (v) uniform positive-twist projective generation. Serre's proof needs (iv) explicitly, not just (iii). His Lemma7 supplies positive-twist vanishing on the lower-dimensional hyperplane by dimension induction through already established lower-dimensional GAGA and algebraic Serre vanishing. Thus full independent analytic Serre vanishing in all dimensions is not needed before the induction; assuming GAGA in the same dimension would be circular.

## Actual source retrieval and reading limits

No PDF or extracted-source file was written. HTTP requests and PyMuPDF extraction were performed in memory.

* Serre, *Géométrie algébrique et géométrie analytique*: https://www.college-de-france.fr/media/jean-pierre-serre/UPL1698785858825941763_Serre_GAGA.pdf . HTTP 200; 3,620,462 bytes; 43 PDF pages; SHA256 `eaba41b5104642135aea9418245fee3a6e38faa593fdaa7cd002e1b962d93e1f`. Actually read PDF pp.5–28 and 35–43 (printed pp.4–27,34–42), including §3 coherence discussion, §6 local comparison, §9 exactness/coherence, §§12–17 theorem statements and proofs, Annex §§21–24 and bibliography. Pages1–4 and29–34 were not read in this investigation. The source is in French; extraction contains OCR corruption. No claimed reading of sources merely cited in Serre, including Cartan–Serre's 1953 note or Cartan seminars.
* Demailly, *Complex Analytic and Differential Geometry*: https://www-fourier.univ-grenoble-alpes.fr/~demailly/manuscripts/agbook.pdf . HTTP200; 3,557,990 bytes; 455 PDF pages; SHA256 `d7c7654a7417e8322e5dcf8fe8ec818b4c1a18cf280b41f2df5a871b776d89a1`. Actually read complete printed/PDF pp.89–90 (II§3.3, Oka Theorem3.19, Lemma3.20 and proof), pp.347–349 (VII§10 line-bundle computations), pp.377–379 (VIII§6,6.4–6.9), pp.406–408 (IX§1, Schwartz1.8, compact-complex theorem1.9, beginning Mittag-Leffler1.11), pp.419–428 (IX§4, local coherent vanishing, Fréchet topology, compact restrictions, Cartan–Serre4.8, approximation, Andreotti–Grauert4.10/Cor4.11 and proof). Tables and automated hits on other pages were inspected only for navigation: those are not full proof reading. In particular, no claim that the earlier bundle estimate, nuclear-space theory or all prerequisites of these chapters were reconstructed or read. The queried PDF pp.429–430 only supplied direct-image statement and initial tensor-product definitions, not its proof. This does not discharge A2.

Serre's printed p.24 calls the *positive-twist* Lemma7 “théorème B” of Cartan's projective seminar and Lemma8 “théorème A.” This is a possible origin of the item's false unqualified phrase: these projective twisted statements must not be replaced by the usual untwisted Stein A/B.

## Imported supplier inventory and limits

The following nine actual bytes were SHA256-checked against `research/math-imports.json`; all matched. Full text of the first two, smooth bounded solver, Weierstrass division, germ Noetherianity and completion items was inspected; for the long global Hörmander/corollary files the complete statement and the cited proof boundary were inspected, without claiming an independent audit of every transitive premise.

