          "id": "step-4-1",
          "step": "4.1",
          "claim": "To obtain derivative decay, fix $\\alpha<\\alpha'<\\sqrt\\kappa$ and use step 3.3 at rate $\\alpha'$. On each unit ball centered at large $z$, both $w$ and $\\Delta w=\\kappa(1-e^{-w})$ are $O(e^{-\\alpha'|z|})$. By [F3] and [F5], $w$ has a $C^{1,\\beta}$ norm of that order on the concentric half-ball for some $\\beta>0$. Thus the right-hand side has a $C^{0,\\beta}$ norm of the same order, and [F4] gives $C^{2,\\beta}$ decay on a smaller ball. Inductively, for each multi-index $\\gamma$, differentiating $\\Delta w=\\kappa(1-e^{-w})$ gives $\\Delta D^\\gamma w=\\kappa e^{-w}D^\\gamma w+G_\\gamma$, where $G_\\gamma$ is a finite sum of products of lower derivatives of $w$ and is exponentially small by the induction hypothesis. Applying [F3] and [F4] on nested unit balls gives the same $e^{-\\alpha'|z|}$ bound for two more derivatives. Since $e^{-\\alpha'|z|}\\le e^{-\\alpha|z|}$ outside a fixed disk, every finite derivative has the stated rate.",
          "inputs": [
