items/ex-qftx-gaga-analytic-relation-kernel.md:56:## Facts & Assumptions
items/ex-qftx-gaga-analytic-relation-kernel.md:60:[A1] [[def-axiom-of-choice]]: AC is the theorem's adopted ambient assumption.
items/ex-qftx-gaga-analytic-relation-kernel.md:62:[F1] [[def-qftx-analytic-coherent-module]]: the relation sheaf is the kernel of $\mu$, and local finite generation means one finite family generates all stalks on a neighborhood.
items/ex-qftx-gaga-analytic-relation-kernel.md:64:[F6] [[def-stalk-of-presheaf]]: a stalk consists of germs of sections on neighborhoods of the point.
items/ex-qftx-gaga-analytic-relation-kernel.md:66:[F2] [[thm-qftx-gaga-analytic-oka-coherence]]: $\mathcal O_D$ is coherent and every finite tuple has a locally finite-type relation sheaf.
items/ex-qftx-gaga-analytic-relation-kernel.md:68:[F3] [[lem-qftx-coherent-analytic-module-calculus]]: kernels and finite extensions of coherent modules are coherent.
items/ex-qftx-gaga-analytic-relation-kernel.md:70:[F4] [[thm-exactness-of-sheaves-stalkwise]]: equality of the explicit generated subsheaf with the kernel sheaf is checked stalkwise.
items/ex-qftx-gaga-analytic-relation-kernel.md:72:[F5] [[thm-power-series-expansion-in-several-complex-variables]] and [[cor-uniqueness-of-multivariable-power-series-coefficients]]: holomorphic germs have convergent power series with unique coefficients, and the ring of such germs has no zero divisors by multiplying first nonzero homogeneous terms.
items/ex-qftx-gaga-analytic-relation-kernel.md:76:1.1 Fix $x=(x_1,x_2)\in D$ with $x\ne0$. If $z_1(x)\ne0$, then $z_1$ is a unit germ and a relation $z_1a+z_2b=0$ satisfies $(a,b)=(b/z_1)(-z_2,z_1)$. If $z_1(x)=0$, then $z_2(x)\ne0$, so $z_2$ is a unit germ and $(a,b)=(-a/z_2)(-z_2,z_1)$. Thus the stated section generates every relation stalk away from the origin. [A1, F1, F6, given, algebra]
items/ex-qftx-gaga-analytic-relation-kernel.md:78:2.1 At the origin, let $a z_1+b z_2=0$ as a holomorphic germ. Restricting to $z_1=0$ gives $z_2b(0,z_2)=0$ as a one-variable germ, so [F5] makes $b(0,z_2)=0$. Write the convergent series $b(z_1,z_2)=\sum_{m,n\ge0}c_{mn}z_1^mz_2^n$. Uniqueness of coefficients makes $c_{0n}=0$ for every $n$, so $b=z_1c$ for the holomorphic germ $c=\sum_{m\ge1,n\ge0}c_{mn}z_1^{m-1}z_2^n$. [F5, given, algebra]
items/ex-qftx-gaga-analytic-relation-kernel.md:80:2.2 Substituting $b=z_1c$ into the relation gives $z_1(a+z_2c)=0$. The germ ring is a domain by [F5], so $a=-z_2c$ and $(a,b)=c(-z_2,z_1)$. Hence the same section generates the relation stalk at the origin. [step 2.1, F5, algebra]
items/ex-qftx-gaga-analytic-relation-kernel.md:82:3.1 Steps 1.1 and 2.2 show that the generated subsheaf and $\ker\mu$ have equal stalks at every point, where a stalk is the germ module from [F6]; [F4] identifies them. Therefore the relation sheaf is locally of finite type. By [F2], $\mathcal O_D$ is coherent; $\mathcal O_D^{\oplus2}$ is coherent by the split short exact sequence $0\to\mathcal O_D\to\mathcal O_D^{\oplus2}\to\mathcal O_D\to0$ and [F3]. Applying [F3] to $\mu$ shows that its kernel is coherent. [F2, F3, F4, F6, step 1.1, step 2.2]
