items/lem-qftx-coherent-analytic-module-calculus.md:44:## Facts & Assumptions
items/lem-qftx-coherent-analytic-module-calculus.md:48:[F1] [[def-qftx-analytic-coherent-module]]: a coherent module is locally of finite type, and the kernel of every morphism from a finite-rank free module sheaf into it is locally of finite type.
items/lem-qftx-coherent-analytic-module-calculus.md:50:[F2] [[def-kernel-cokernel-image-sheaves]]: kernels are objectwise; cokernel and image sheaves are the sheafifications of their sectionwise presheaves.
items/lem-qftx-coherent-analytic-module-calculus.md:52:[F3] [[def-exact-sequence-sheaves]]: a short exact sequence has zero kernel at the left endpoint, image equal to kernel at the middle term, and zero cokernel at the right endpoint.
items/lem-qftx-coherent-analytic-module-calculus.md:54:[F4] [[thm-exactness-of-sheaves-stalkwise]]: epimorphisms and exactness in the constructions below can be checked on stalks.
items/lem-qftx-coherent-analytic-module-calculus.md:58:1.1 Let $\mathcal F$ be coherent and fix $x\in X$. Local finite type gives, after choosing a neighborhood $U$ of $x$, a finite-rank free module sheaf map $\pi:\mathcal O_U^{\oplus k}\to\mathcal F|_U$ that is surjective on every stalk. By [F1], its kernel is locally of finite type; after shrinking to $V\subseteq U$, choose finitely many sections generating that kernel on $V$ and let $\rho:\mathcal O_V^{\oplus m}\to\mathcal O_V^{\oplus k}$ be the corresponding map. The sequence $\mathcal O_V^{\oplus m}\xrightarrow{\rho}\mathcal O_V^{\oplus k}\xrightarrow{\pi}\mathcal F|_V\to0$ is exact by [F2], [F3], and [F4]. Thus every coherent module has a local finite presentation. [F1, F2, F3, F4, given, construct]
items/lem-qftx-coherent-analytic-module-calculus.md:60:2.1 Let $f:\mathcal F\to\mathcal G$ be a morphism of coherent modules and set $\mathcal K=\ker f$. Choose locally a finite-rank free epimorphism $\pi:\mathcal O^{\oplus k}\to\mathcal F$. The composite $f\pi:\mathcal O^{\oplus k}\to\mathcal G$ has a locally finite-type kernel by [F1]; its image under $\pi$ is exactly $\mathcal K$ on each stalk, since $\pi$ is stalkwise surjective. Hence $\mathcal K$ is locally of finite type by [F4]. For every finite-rank map $\eta:\mathcal O^{\oplus p}\to\mathcal K$, its composite with the inclusion $\mathcal K\hookrightarrow\mathcal F$ has the same kernel; [F1] for $\mathcal F$ makes that kernel locally of finite type. Thus $\mathcal K$ is coherent. [F1, F2, F4, step 1.1, given]
items/lem-qftx-coherent-analytic-module-calculus.md:62:3.1 Let $\mathcal C=\operatorname{coker}f$. It is locally of finite type because it is a quotient of the locally finite-type module $\mathcal G$. To check its relation condition, fix a finite-rank map $\gamma:\mathcal O^{\oplus p}\to\mathcal C$ and a point $x$. Since $\mathcal G\to\mathcal C$ is a sheaf epimorphism, choose local lifts of the finitely many images of the standard basis near $x$; they define $\widetilde\gamma:\mathcal O^{\oplus p}\to\mathcal G$ lifting $\gamma$. Also choose a local finite-rank epimorphism $\delta:\mathcal O^{\oplus m}\to\mathcal F$. Define $\epsilon:\mathcal O^{\oplus(m+p)}\to\mathcal G$ by $\epsilon(a,b)=f(\delta(a))+\widetilde\gamma(b)$. By [F1], $\ker\epsilon$ is locally of finite type. Projection of $\ker\epsilon$ to the second factor has image exactly $\ker\gamma$ on every stalk: an element of $\ker\epsilon$ maps to zero in $\mathcal C$, and any stalk element $b\in\ker\gamma$ has $\widetilde\gamma(b)\in\operatorname{im}f$, so a stalk preimage under $\delta$ completes it to an element of $\ker\epsilon$. The image of a locally finite-type module is locally finite type, so $\ker\gamma$ is locally of finite type. This holds for every $\gamma$, hence $\mathcal C$ is coherent. [F1, F2, F4, step 1.1, construct]
items/lem-qftx-coherent-analytic-module-calculus.md:64:4.1 Consider a short exact sequence $0\to\mathcal F'\xrightarrow{i}\mathcal E\xrightarrow{p}\mathcal F''\to0$. If $\mathcal E$ and $\mathcal F''$ are coherent, then $\mathcal F'=\ker p$ is coherent by step 2.1. If $\mathcal F'$ and $\mathcal E$ are coherent, then $\mathcal F''=\operatorname{coker}i$ is coherent by step 3.1. [F2, F3, step 2.1, step 3.1]
items/lem-qftx-coherent-analytic-module-calculus.md:66:4.2 It remains to assume $\mathcal F'$ and $\mathcal F''$ coherent. Local finite generators of $\mathcal F'$ together with local lifts to $\mathcal E$ of finite generators of $\mathcal F''$ generate $\mathcal E$, so $\mathcal E$ is locally of finite type. For any finite-rank map $g:\mathcal O^{\oplus k}\to\mathcal E$, the kernel of $pg$ is locally of finite type by [F1] for $\mathcal F''$; choose a local finite-rank epimorphism $\gamma:\mathcal O^{\oplus m}\to\ker(pg)$. Exactness gives a map $\delta:\mathcal O^{\oplus m}\to\mathcal F'$ with $i\delta=g\gamma$. By [F1] for $\mathcal F'$, $\ker\delta$ is locally of finite type. On each stalk, $\gamma$ maps $\ker\delta$ onto $\ker g$: inclusion follows from $i\delta=g\gamma$, and if $s\in\ker g$, then $pg(s)=0$, so $s=\gamma(t)$ for some $t$ and $i\delta(t)=g(s)=0$; injectivity of $i$ gives $\delta(t)=0$. Therefore $\ker g$ is locally of finite type. Since this holds for every $g$, $\mathcal E$ is coherent. [F1, F2, F3, F4, step 4.1, algebra, construct] ∎
items/lem-qftx-gaga-analytic-bounded-degree-relations.md:9:dependency_level: 1
