  "steps": [
    {
      "id": "1.1",
      "text": "If $y\\in D$ is not the origin, choose an index $k$ with $z_k(y)\\ne0$. Then $z_k$ is a unit in the germ ring $\\mathcal O_{D,y}$, so the ideal generated by the coordinates is the whole stalk and $\\mathcal F_y=0$. [F4, F6, given, choose]"
    },
    {
      "id": "1.2",
      "text": "At the origin, evaluation $\\operatorname{ev}_0:\\mathcal O_{D,0}\\to\\mathbb C$ is surjective. Its kernel is generated by $z_1,\\ldots,z_N$: if $f(0)=0$, its convergent power series has no constant term, and grouping each nonconstant monomial according to the first coordinate with positive exponent writes $f=\\sum_i z_i g_i$ with convergent germs $g_i$; each of the finitely many grouped subseries remains convergent on a smaller polydisc. Conversely every such sum vanishes at $0$. Hence $\\mathcal F_0\\cong\\mathbb C$. [F4, F5, F6, algebra]"
